# Testing & Quality Assurance

## Three-Tier Verification Gate

Every code or documentation change flows through an escalating **Tier 1 -> Tier 1.5 -> Tier 2** verification funnel:

### Tier 1 — Deterministic Gate (`make check` / `make check-fast`)

Local linters, typecheckers, and deterministic automated tests run first. Any Tier 1 failure short-circuits immediately before semantic review:

- **Static Quality Gates**: [e.g. `codespell`, `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `pyright` — run via `make lint` or `make check`.]
- **Unit Tests**: [Fast, deterministic, offline tests mocking external APIs and persistence.]
- **Integration & E2E Tests**: [Tests exercising live or emulated cloud services, containers, or full HTTP servers.]
- **Frontend / Agent Evals**: [Component/UI test runners or ADK evaluation suites, where applicable.]

### Tier 1.5 — Calibrated Decision Rubric (`make rubric-dry` / `make rubric`)

Evaluates non-`[det]` assertions (`B1`–`Bn` from [docs/SPEC.md](SPEC.md)) in a single zero-output-token prefill pass via `gemini-decision-1` (`eval_rubric.py`, passing e.g. `RUBRIC_ARGS="--base main"`):

- Skips `[det]` gates already proved by Tier 1 shell exit codes.
- Terminates clear mechanical/`[ui]` passes without spawning a subagent, and fails fast (`FAIL_FAST`) on clear omissions.
- Marks `[arch]` invariants as `PROVISIONAL_ARCH_PASS` for final Tier 2 review.
- Degrades gracefully to `Tier 1 -> Tier 2` when `GEMINI_API_KEY` is absent (exit `3`).

### Tier 2 — Stateless Semantic Critic

A fresh, read-only reviewer subagent (with zero prior coding chain-of-thought) invoked only on Tier 1.5 grey-zone escalations or for one final sign-off on `[arch]` assertions once Tier 1 and Tier 1.5 are clear.

## Local vs CI Execution

- **CI Mode (`CI=true`)**: [Non-interactive execution, skipping local `.env` loading, watch mode disabled, log-optimised output.]
- **Test Mode & Fixtures**: [Global `conftest.py` configuration, environment variable guards, and mock client/token patterns.]

## Test Suite Inventory

| File / Path | Tier | Scope & Behaviours Verified |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `tests/unit/[test_file.py]` | Unit | [Core behaviours and edge cases verified] |
| `tests/integration/[test_file.py]` | Integration | [External boundary or multi-component behaviour verified] |

## Running Tests

- **Full Offline Verification**: `make check`
- **Unit Suite Only**: `make test`
- **Unit + Integration**: `make test-all`
- **Targeted File**: `uv run pytest -v tests/unit/[test_file.py]`
- **Tier 1.5 Offline Dry-Run**: `make rubric-dry`
- **Tier 1.5 Live Screen**: `make rubric` (pass `RUBRIC_ARGS="--base main"` for PR branches)

